  "title": "The Route Has More Than One Sense",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "accessibility/inclusion",
  "premise": "A museum wants visitors to find a gallery, but directions rely only on a spoken announcement. A co-designed prototype pairs clear text, visual landmarks, and other appropriate cues so visitors can choose useful information.",
  "hook": "What if the announcement is not available to you?",
  "visible_action": "One audio path branches into text signage, a visual map, and a reviewed tactile-cue mockup leading to the same destination.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Important wayfinding information can be offered through complementary modes.",
  "gate": "Consult users and qualified access guidance; do not improvise tactile standards or emergency routes.",
